<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baraqish</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yathill</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baraqish, ancient Yathill, is a walled ruined city in the al-Jawf region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, north-east of Sanaa. It was the second city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-main">Kingdom of Ma'in</a> and a station on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incense">incense</a> route, enclosed by stone walls with dozens of towers. In 25–24 BCE the Roman expedition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aelius-gallus">Aelius Gallus</a> took it on its way towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marib">Marib</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baraqish.jpg" alt="Baraqish" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: txago · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barakisk_flickr01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
